Design: We will fine-tune a pretrained DenseNet121 for binary classification (malignant vs benign/non-neoplastic), splitting the data 80/20 stratified by malignancy. We apply standard augmentations (random resized crop, flips) on training data and center‐crop plus normalization on validation. We train for 5 epochs using BCEWithLogitsLoss and Adam optimizer, tracking validation AUROC and saving the best model. Finally, we implement a predict(folder_path) function that loads the saved model and returns malignancy probabilities for all images in the specified folder.
